        public const string PluginVersion = "0.2.1224";   // 0.2.1224 ([lead], Fire 11-10): the day / time box under the minimap is off unless a mod provides its setting (fallback was on). 0.2.1223 ([generator], lead / [worldgen] 11-10): the ground-snow step waits while Vedr is installed but its season is not ready yet (no cover change), instead of assuming full winter (season 1), which marked winter snow as fallen for a world that ticked before Vedr was ready; it runs on the first frame Vedr is ready. One Debug line. No keys. // 0.2.1222 ([generator], lead 11-09, Fire's snow on the clean world): environment boxes hold the snow globals (_GlobalSnowAmount, _SnowAmount, _AddSnow) as one shared owner set; the true values are captured once by the first snow box and put back only when the last one lets go, so nested or overlapping boxes, any exit order, an unload, a teleport or fly-out never leave snow at 1. Each global is restored to its own original (was: _SnowAmount got _GlobalSnowAmount's, _AddSnow forced 0). OnDestroy exits for any box the player is in and always lets go; every box the player is in is validated, not only the last one entered; leaving the current box while still in another makes that box current. Debug owner-count line. No keys. // 0.2.1221 ([ghost], frozen by [generator]; same public hitch report, next pass): Core's companion and snow code no longer searches the whole scene. ColdRisk / ChoreBrainBase / SnowFires (fires), HomesteadDefence / ChoreBrainBase (beds), OreNeed (smelters) and SnowChores (doors / smelters / beds) read station lists filled at each Awake. SnowChores roofs and stations read vanilla's own lists (WearNTear.GetAllInstances, CraftingStation.m_allStations), and CompanionPatches' six companion searches read CompanionController.AllCompanions (active ones, copied). The fire list's Awake hook is ungated, so snow melt works with the companion brain off. Beds and doors join the 1220 lists (same bounded purge). Distance is checked before the costly tests (IsBurning, the roof raycast); same answers. Each list is used only while the patch that fills it is active, otherwise the old search; one Info line per list says which. Key [Performance] Scene scans from registries (default on; off = the old searches, for an A/B). Debug [ScanCensus] every 60 s: calls, items walked and ms per site. // 0.2.1220 ([ghost], frozen by [generator]; public bug report via Fire 11-08: a 33-90 ms hitch every 10 s, growing with mod count, even with no companions): HomesteadNeeds builds only when need-based chore scores (or its summary log) are on AND the local player has a tamed companion, and its CoreSettings key [Homestead Needs] Needs model (default on) turns it off outright. Otherwise it does nothing, with one Debug line saying why. The four scene-wide FindObjectsByType calls (smelters / kilns, plants, cooking stations, fires) are replaced by station lists filled at each station's Awake (Npc\JobBoard\HomesteadStations.cs; destroyed entries dropped as met, and purged on growth so they stay bounded while the model is idle), and the rebuild runs one phase per Job Board tick (2 s apart) instead of all at once. Debug 60 s census (registered stations, worst phase ms). // 0.2.1219 ([generator], Fire 11-08: rendering / perf only in FGN / EBM / FiresFixes; ships in the SAME slot as EBM 1.2.210, which runs the far view itself): Core's Far\ folder (ImpostorEngine / ImpostorDraw, FarCache, FarLights, FarBuildings + digest, FarRunner, MeshSimplify) and its embedded firescoreimpostor bundle are removed (two copies of that bundle cannot load in one process). FAP 1.1.411 / FAT 0.2.1425 look the Core types up quietly and stand down. No keys. // 0.2.1218 ([generator], PLAN_CoreToEbmApi section B; EBM 1.2.208): Core reads EBM stand-ins through EbmApi instead of EBM internals. Compat\EbmStandIns binds EbmApi.StandInPrefab(Collider) and the StandInsChanged(zone, left) event by type name. SnowShelterEbm subscribes to it at CoreLateOwners.RunOnce