tureSkip (type name only, run once from CoreLateOwners.RunOnce); World\DistantSectorSkip and Lifecycle\CollisionCallbackReuse removed from Core (FiresFixes carries both). SectorChanges stays (public; on [wishbone]'s inventory). + FIX (Fire 11-08 615 y53, "still not rendering the builds at the back of the town on the hill"; client "server sent 20 zone(s), 0 applied"): FarBuildingDigest's fingerprint hashed the rotation as RoundToInt(eulerAngles.y*10) while the wire/cache carry four int16s, so the receiver's recomputed print differed (yaw on a rounding edge or at the 0/360 wrap) and every such zone was dropped whole, server zones and cached zones alike; the print now hashes the exact int16s written, and the receive line names how many zones were loaded here / rejected and why. Server and client must both run 1216; caches written by older builds re-fill from the server / scans. No keys. // 0.2.1215 ([generator], Fire 11-08 "fgn better not rely on core for anything"; FGN 1.6.63 FgnApi v8): Npc\FgnHooksBridge.cs, run once from CoreLateOwners.RunOnce before KinematicSync decides: Core registers FGN's stats card (FgnApi.GetStatsRows mapped to StatRow), registers FgnApi.RegisterFarIdleSkip so FGN never far-idles a Core companion, and provides FGN's Kinematic sync sweep value (FgnApi.KinematicSweepEnabled) to CoreSettings at priority 10. Type name only, no reference either way; without FGN v8 one Debug line. No keys. // 0.2.1214 ([generator], Fire 11-08 "fgn better not rely on core for anything"): FGN no longer reads Core; Core registers its companion keep (CompanionKeep.Refresh / IsKept) into FGN's own hook FgnApi.RegisterServerRemovalKeep (FGN 1.6.62, API v7) on every ZNet.Awake, found by type name only (Npc\FgnRemovalKeepBridge.cs), owner = Core's Harmony id. Without FGN nothing happens. No keys. // 0.2.1213 ([generator], lead / [fgn] 11-08: FGN 1.6.60's sliced server removal fell back to the whole RemoveObjects every 2 s, 17-20 ms): the companion keep as data - TamedCompanionZoneLoader.RemoveObjects_Prefix's body moved unchanged into CollectKept(list), which the prefix calls; add-only FiresCore.Npc.CompanionKeep { Active, Version, Refresh(), IsKept(ZDO) } fills its set from the same CollectKept, so FGN can stay sliced and keep exactly what the prefix keeps. Server only; no keys. // 0.2.1212 ([ghost], DESIGN_OcclusionLOD §5, lead 11-08): Far\MeshSimplify, Core's one grid-cluster mesh simplifier made public (FarBuildingMerge now calls it; EBM's intact-rock LOD1 reuses it by name). No behaviour change. // 0.2.1211 ([wishbone] on [visual]'s 1210, lead 11-08, [generator]'s piece-create audit rows 2 / 5 / 12, TOWN50): Core's per-piece snow hooks (WearNTear Awake/OnDestroy SnowGround, Piece Awake/OnDestroy Shelter) read one bool worked out once per frame (the key + the owner) instead of a SnowConfig.P string lookup + lock per piece, and do nothing while Vedr owns the ground snow (Vedr runs its own copies); the shelter marks a zone once per frame in a zone fill; ownership back to Core re-marks the loaded zones. GravityBody's ZNetView.Awake Rigidbody lookup runs only while a gravity field is active (GravityUp.Active); bodies created before a field appears are picked up once. Not unpatched at runtime: an unpatch rebuilds the shared Awake methods with every other mod's patches. No keys.   // 0.2.1210 ([visual] on [ghost]'s 1209, lead 11-08, TOWN50 / Fire shots 613-615): (a) FarFarBuildingDigest: a client also reads the ZDOs it HOLDS for zones it has not loaded, out to [Far buildings] Reach (was loaded zones within 400 m), additively (a held scan adds or updates pieces, never removes one), so the far BlueHills keep draws from the 615 spot; Debug "[FarBuildings] digest, last 30 s: ... held-zone scan(s) (N zone(s) grew, +P piece(s) from held ZDOs)". (b) MaterialsPinkCensus: the Debug-only census (a 256 ms hitch frame in cell 0) takes one unsorted scene-only snapshot and walks it 512 renderers a step through Core's FrameBudgetScheduler (Low lane)